cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study, its data or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "Calibration Atlas: a reproducible calibration study of resolved Polymarket markets"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Guinerve
repository-code: "https://github.com/Guinerve/calibration-atlas"
url: "https://guinerve.github.io/calibration-atlas/"
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
keywords:
  - prediction markets
  - calibration
  - forecasting
  - Polymarket
  - preregistration
abstract: >-
  A calibration study of 11,881 resolved Polymarket markets from the 1,500 closed events with
  the most trading (January 2024 to October 2026). It fits recalibration slopes with errors
  clustered by event, pools the category slopes with a Bayesian model, and backtests one trading
  strategy. A holdout test, fixed in advance, checks the macro slope on markets that closed after
  the collection.
